</form><html xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:math="java.lang.Math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions" xmlns:xdt="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-datatypes" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>ACA23:v99#DOCUMENT</title><meta name="dc:identifier" content="ACA23"/><meta name="dc:title" content="ACA &#xA;              23-&#xA;                INTRODUCED&#xA;              "/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/></head><body><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Start</h2></span><div id="bill_all" align="justify"><div id="about"><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td align="center"/></tr></tbody></table></div><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><font size="3" style="FONT-FAMILY: MinionPC, Arial Unicode MS">
                    CALIFORNIA LEGISLATURE—
                    2025–2026 REGULAR SESSION</font></div><br clear="all"/><span id="bill_house_num"><div style="float: left; width:50%; font-weight: bold; "><span style="text-transform: uppercase; text-align:left;width:50%;"><b>
                Assembly Constitutional Amendment
              </b></span></div><div style="float:right; width:50%; text-align:right;"><span style="text-transform: uppercase;"><b>No. 23</b></span></div></span><hr/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td id="bill_authors" align="center"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Introduced by Assembly Members Johnson and Hoover<br/></span></td></tr><tr><td id="bill_intro_date" align="center" class="textcenter"><br/>August 10, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr/><br clear="all"/><div id="title"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-size:0.9em;"> A resolution to propose to the people of the State of California an amendment to the Constitution of the State, by amending Section 6 of Article II thereof, relating to elections. </span></div><br clear="all"/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><h2>LEGISLATIVE COUNSEL'S DIGEST</h2></div><br/><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0"><span id="subject">ACA 23, as introduced, Johnson.
                          Secretary of State: nonpartisan office.</span></div><div><span id="digesttext"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">The California Constitution establishes the office of Secretary of State and requires that the Secretary of State be elected at the same time and place and for the same term as the Governor. The California Constitution provides that all judicial, school, county, and city offices, and the office of Superintendent of Public Instruction, are nonpartisan. The California Constitution prohibits a political party or party central committee from nominating a candidate for nonpartisan office, and prohibits the candidate’s party preference from being included on the ballot.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">This measure would additionally provide that the office of Secretary of State is a nonpartisan office.</div></span></div><span class="hidden"><h2>Digest Key</h2></span><span id="vote">
      Vote:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">2/3</span>  </span><span id="appropriation">
      Appropriation:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">NO</span>  </span><span id="fiscalcommittee">
      Fiscal Committee:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">NO</span>  </span><span id="localprogram">
      Local Program:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">NO</span>  </span></div><hr/><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Text</h2></span><span class="Resolution" title="source: /caml:MeasureDoc/caml:Resolution&#xA;    "><span class="Resolved" id="id_75A1E20B-CAAA-4D12-9389-ABBE727616AB"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved by the Assembly, the Senate concurring, That the Legislature of the State of California at its 2025–26 Regular Session, commencing on the second day of December 2024, two-thirds of the membership of each house concurring, hereby proposes to the people of the State of California that the Constitution of the State be amended as follows:</div><div id="s20.9552370105322758"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0" class="ActionLine"><h3 style="font-weight:bold; display:inline;"/> That Section 6 of Article II thereof is amended to read:</div><div><div id="id_01656D03-B14F-415D-943A-5E8A2C804F57"><div><p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"><h6 style="display:inline;">SEC. 6.</h6> (a) <font color="#B30000"><strike>All judicial, school, county, and city offices, including the Superintendent of Public Instruction, </strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i>The following offices </i></font>shall be<font color="#B30000"><strike> nonpartisan.</strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i> nonpartisan:</i></font></div><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;margin-left: 1em;">(1) All judicial, school, county, and city offices.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;margin-left: 1em;">(2) Superintendent of Public Instruction.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;margin-left: 1em;">(3) Secretary of State.</div></i></font><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(b) A political party or party central committee shall not nominate a candidate for nonpartisan office, and the candidate’s party preference shall not be included on the ballot for the nonpartisan office.</div></p></div></div></div></div></span></span></div></body></html>
